{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/658408-incarnates-questions","id":658408,"title":"Incarnates questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T14:56:30-07:00","id":658408,"title":"Incarnates questions","content":"Since Incarnate Inheritance is very much a transcendent condition for Beasts that harmoniously fuses the two sides of their existence, and Horrors are ageless spiritual creatures, I wonder if it should bestow immortality to characters that attain it, in the sense of immunity to age and mundane diseases at least, or the Incarnate just gets the longevity bonus that comes with very high Lair. It would seem there is plenty of thematic justification for the Myth to suspend the Beast's mortality as long as it holds strong and true, but then again I'm quite biased in favor of immortal characters to begin with.<br /> <br /> Most benefits of Adopting the Beast-Shape seem similar to the ones of many Atavisms. Are their effects supposed to be stackable ?<br /> <br /> How is an Incarnate Beast supposed to re-stabilize its Myth if it gets destabilized ? Removing the conditions that threatened it ? Repeating the mythic feat that allowed it to claim the Inheritance in the first place, or an equivalent one ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T18:59:07-07:00","id":658762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/658408-incarnates-questions#post658408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Incarnate Inheritance is very much a transcendent condition for Beasts that harmoniously fuses the two sides of their existence, and Horrors are ageless spiritual creatures, I wonder if it should bestow immortality to characters that attain it, in the sense of immunity to age and mundane diseases at least, or the Incarnate just gets the longevity bonus that comes with very high Lair. It would seem there is plenty of thematic justification for the Myth to suspend the Beast's mortality as long as it holds strong and true, but then again I'm quite biased in favor of immortal characters to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most benefits of Adopting the Beast-Shape seem similar to the ones of many Atavisms. Are their effects supposed to be stackable ? </div> </div> </div>Sure, why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is an Incarnate Beast supposed to re-stabilize its Myth if it gets destabilized ? Removing the conditions that threatened it ? Repeating the mythic feat that allowed it to claim the Inheritance in the first place, or an equivalent one ? </div> </div> </div>Either of those seem workable to me. All follows the same pattern, showing your dominance, and establishing others, especially heroes, as minor characters in your story, rather than the other way around. Remind people why they feared you in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","user":"WarDragon","date":". 09-10-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}